Region allocators are noncopyable and `deallocateAll()` is `@system`

`Region`, `BorrowedRegion`, `SharedRegion`, and `SharedBorrowedRegion` no longer
allow copying. Copies duplicate allocation cursors and can return overlapping
blocks with incompatible types; owning regions also duplicate responsibility
for releasing their backing storage. Pass these allocators by reference instead
of copying them. `InSituRegion` was already noncopyable.

`deallocateAll()` is explicitly `@system` for these types and `InSituRegion`.
It invalidates every outstanding allocation, and the allocator cannot prove
that callers have stopped using all aliases before storage is reused.
